{
  "id": 164586930,
  "iid": 7368,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "IEEE 802.15.4: Add support for Rendez Vous Time IE and CSL Wake Up Frames (#18182)",
  "description": "Fixes #18182.\n\nThis adds support for the Rendez Vous Time IE and updates the CSL Wake-Up Frame packet information, as follows:\n![image](/uploads/e59f8fba33996204431ea81255b8fdcf/image.png)\n\nAccording to my reading, the spec is unclear on whether the \"Wake up Interval\" field is optional or not. \n- The table does not use the \"0/2\" convention, thus indicating it is not optional\n- The text says \"only present when macCslInterval is nonzero\"\n\nThe proposed change assumes the field is optional.\n\nThe \"RendezVous Time\" field currently (as of 802.15.4-2015) has the same definition as used in the CSL IE, so my commit reuses it. But I am open to suggestions if you think it is better to redefine it, in case it changes in the future.\n\nReference capture:\n[csl_wake_up_frame.pcapng.gz](/uploads/34d0bfbeb3f5fe5efa0eb415e544f97b/csl_wake_up_frame.pcapng.gz)\n\nFuzzy-tested on my machine against the contributed capture file: no issues after 80+ passes:\n```\n../tools/fuzz-test.sh ~/downloads/csl_wake_up_frame.pcapng.gz\nASan enabled. Virtual memory limit is unlimited\nRunning run/tshark  with args: \"-nVxr\" \"-nr\" (forever)\n\nPass 1:\n    csl_wake_up_frame.pcapng.gz: (-nVxr) (-nr)  OK (2 seconds)\n...\nPass 87:\n    csl_wake_up_frame.pcapng.gz: (-nVxr) (-nr)  OK (1 seconds)\n```",
  "state": "merged",
